[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3041951948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-3041951948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":3041951948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61UIDM","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-06T15:17:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-06T15:17:40Z","body":"This is already an available option. In order to prevent this, you need to add a RESET animation, as noted in the [reset_on_save property of AnimationMixer](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_animationmixer.html#class-animationmixer-property-reset-on-save).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3041951948/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3045441843","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-3045441843","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":3045441843,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61hcEz","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T14:33:10Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T14:33:10Z","body":"This does indeed look by design, you are changing the values, so they should be saved, and as suggested above the solution is to use reset on save to ensure a clean state","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3045441843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056701638","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-3056701638","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":3056701638,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62MZDG","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T10:03:11Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T10:03:11Z","body":"I had a look at my project and Reset on Save is checked.\n\nI am speaking about characters that I import with their animations from Blender, and it seems that:\n- they are imported with `Reset on Save` checked by default\n- RESET animation is not added automatically by Godot\n- I don't see an option to add a RESET animation\n\nI think the users should not have to worry about adding manually a RESET animation. Godot could just add it itself?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056701638/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057314144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-3057314144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":3057314144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62Oulg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T12:48:07Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T12:48:07Z","body":"You can set up reset tracks in your Blender project, the importer supports handling them, that's probably good practice","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057314144/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057798007","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-3057798007","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":3057798007,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62Qkt3","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T14:51:20Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T14:51:20Z","body":"I don't use tracks to save time and keep my blender file simple. \nI just create actions like so, which I export with the GLTF exporter:\n\n<img width=\"608\" height=\"304\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/320ff9ec-8736-4975-86f3-fdf655c43050\" />\n\nBlender has a Reset Position and you can ask the exporter to reset between animations.\nBut I am not sure the reset position is exported to the GLTF.\n\nI still think it would make our life easier if Godot create a RESET animation when it does not exist and the `Reset on Save` is checked.\n\nIf I make a `reset` action in Blender, how do I tell Godot which animation to use as the `RESET` animation? Do I just need to name it `RESET`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057798007/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057811985","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-3057811985","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":3057811985,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62QoIR","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T14:55:06Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T14:55:06Z","body":"That sounds like more of an issue with the blender side of conversion, would be good to make sure you haven't missed any settings\n\nBut adding an option to scene imports to create resets somehow would help, but the problem is how to decide what the reset value should be\n\nA track with the name `RESET` will work, don't know about actions so might not work the same but if it's converted to a track with the same name it should work, or `reset` with the option to add that kind of track enabled in the import settings for scenes","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057811985/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057820796","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-3057820796","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":3057820796,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62QqR8","user":{"login":"Nodragem","id":10520249,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIwMjQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10520249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem","html_url":"https://github.com/Nodragem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nodragem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T14:57:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T14:57:40Z","body":"A default Reset Position is when all bone transformations are cleared. If the user wants something more fancy, they could create their own RESET track.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057820796/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3073338829","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-3073338829","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":3073338829,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63L23N","user":{"login":"martinfelis","id":470116,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDExNg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/470116?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis","html_url":"https://github.com/martinfelis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martinfelis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-15T12:04:24Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T12:04:24Z","body":"@Nodragem have you enabled the \"Import Rest as RESET\" checkbox in the Advanced Import Settings dialog for your animated objects? At least for me ticking this and reimporting the corresponding model causes the RESET animation to be created by Godot automatically.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3073338829/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5259456694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-5259456694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":5259456694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOXzwtg","user":{"login":"Leonardo-Ma","id":68714883,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NzE0ODgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68714883?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma","html_url":"https://github.com/Leonardo-Ma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-11T22:13:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T22:13:56Z","body":"Get default bone position from T-Pose: In your animation player > Open T-Pose > (top right side) Edit > Copy tracks > Select all > Copy.\n\nAdding reset with default bone position: Animation > New > (name) RESET > [Global] > (top right side) Edit > Paste tracks\n\n<img width=\"814\" height=\"395\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5cd20891-ce0e-4667-ae5e-9abf2066329b\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5259456694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5805032206","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108333#issuecomment-5805032206","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108333","id":5805032206,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWgHDDg","user":{"login":"marcospb19","id":38900226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTAwMjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38900226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19","html_url":"https://github.com/marcospb19","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospb19/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-24T00:07:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T00:07:33Z","body":"The problem is that this is updating position+rotation even if I didn't touch anything.\n\nLet me try to re-summarize the entire issue with detailed reproduction steps.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. `git clone https://github.com/godotengine/tps-demo`\n2. `cd tps-demo`\n3. `git reset a82f15448e9b015440d3bbdf5e10801b260c4e9f --hard`\n4. Open Godot editor.\n5. Open `player.tscn` scene.\n6. Save with Ctrl+S\n7. `git diff` to see the rotation+position diff.\n\nThings that didn't solve the issue ❌:\n- Committing the changes (changes again on next save).\n- Toggling `AnimationPlayer`'s child `Active` property.\n- Toggling `AnimationPlayer`'s child `Reset On Save` property.\n- Toggling `Skeleton3D`'s child `Show Rest Only` property.\n\nWhat worked for `player.tscn` ✔️:\n- Reimporting `player.glb` with `Import Rest as RESET` toggled on, and commiting a new rotation/position only once, consecutive saves didn't re-trigger.\n\n(Fix doesn't work for `red_robot.tscn`, it's not getting the `RESET` even after reimporting, I'm still suffering to fix it there.)\n\nTested in:\n- 4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf\n\n---\n\nDealing with this has been very frustrating, what is the point of updating every save? I guess that could be useful if it was a button you can activate, but not as the default behavior.\n\n> This does indeed look by design, you are changing the values\n\nI'm not changing anything here, just saving the scene unchanged (or with unrelated changes), if it's by design then I'd say that I wish that design was reconsidered.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5805032206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]